title: "TransactionExtension::implicit takes the extension version; CheckMetadataHash rejects mode 1 for versions other than 0"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `TransactionExtension::implicit` now takes the extension version of the transaction:
      `fn implicit(&self, extension_version: ExtensionVersion)`. Signed (format 4) transactions
      always pass version `0`. Custom extensions that override `implicit` must add the parameter,
      and wrapper extensions should forward it to the inner extension. Extensions that use the
      default `implicit` need no change.

      `CheckMetadataHash` uses the version to reject `mode = 1` when the extension version is not
      `0`, because the RFC-0078 metadata hash only describes the extensions of version `0`.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      A general transaction that uses an extension version other than `0` with
      `CheckMetadataHash` `mode = 1` is now rejected with `InvalidTransaction::BadProof`. Signed
      transactions and general transactions using extension version `0` are unaffected. `mode = 0`
      is unaffected for every extension version.
crates:
  - name: sp-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: frame-metadata-hash-extension
    bump: patch
  - name: frame-system
    bump: patch
